Z||000000||ArchMagi||04-07-2001||08:15 PM||||I have a bra made by LaBra and i just took it off today so i could wax the front of my car.  My problem is the metal tangs that hold the bra in place are rusted really bad.  Anyone else have this? and what could be a good replacement?<P>Thanks a bunch||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||04-07-2001||08:23 PM||||clean them up as good as possible, wire brush, sandpaper. then get some of that liquid plastic at the hardware store that you use for making grips on tools. just dip it in, let it dry. Bet theres a thousand other parts you could use that stuff on too.<P><BR>Oh, BTW, id throw the bra away myself before it gets to the paint on the front end. My opinion is they do way more harm than any possible good, unless you tailgate people on gravel roads a lot.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 04-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||tgowens||04-07-2001||09:30 PM||||good point Roger!! I just removed one from a Med. Red '87 GT and the paint underneath was all but ruined because the owner left the bra on all the time. As for my own GT's, I only put the bra on when making a road trip with them, then I remove and store it when I get where I am going.........||||reg||1
